1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,542
Meet ShipShape: an autonomous QA crew that lives in Claude Code.

2
00:00:06,683 --> 00:00:07,787
Give it a goal.

3
00:00:07,787 --> 00:00:14,531
It reviews your code and security, then runs every test twice in a real browser, on video.

4
00:00:15,661 --> 00:00:20,821
A refuter attacks every failure, so false alarms never become bugs.

5
00:00:21,151 --> 00:00:25,807
Here it proved the test expected the wrong text, so no bug was filed.

6
00:00:26,937 --> 00:00:31,406
You get one offline report with load results, evidence and trends,

7
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:35,385
delivered to Telegram or WhatsApp only when you say send.

8
00:00:36,515 --> 00:00:41,195
Plain-language hooks block unsafe moves, like a force push to main.

9
00:00:42,325 --> 00:00:47,189
Plus gated desktop control, real timesheets from your Claude Code logs,

10
00:00:47,189 --> 00:00:49,981
and pre-deploy checks for Odoo modules.

11
00:00:51,125 --> 00:00:58,205
Install it in two commands, and watch the full ten minute tutorial to go from zero to self-testing.

